  "description": "PF3 on a screen whose password field is blank and whose CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM is blank. One invocation, two findings.\n\nFirst, UPDATE-USER-INFO takes its FOURTH arm at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:198-203 - the only one no other case in this folder reaches - issuing 'Password can NOT be empty...' with the cursor on PASSWDL, and skipping the read, the change tests and the write entirely. The blank is LOW-VALUES, so this case also carries the 'SPACES OR LOW-VALUES' condition on a third distinct arm.\n\nSecond, PF3 transfers regardless: the error flag does not stop the XCTL, because the return block at :113-119 sits outside any error test. With CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM blank, the IF at :113 is TRUE and 'COADM01C' is moved into CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM - the fallback that sends an operator who arrived from nowhere to the admin menu. Note that the blank-target fallback at :252-253 in RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN itself is DEAD in this program precisely because of that MOVE; it is preserved in the translation as unreachable code rather than deleted, because deleting it would be a change to the program.",
